Vim and configuration

Install:
  Install missing Vim and create ~/.vimrc with line numbers if absent; preserve existing configuration.

Upgrade:
  Update installed Vim; back up and append the line-number setting to existing configuration if the setting is absent.

Status:
  Report the installed package version and whether ~/.vimrc contains the line-number setting.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.

Configuration:
  Configuration: ~/.vimrc
  Upgrade preserves existing lines and does not create an absent configuration file.
